# RTK Command Prefix

Always prefix terminal commands with `rtk`. If RTK has a filter for the command, output is compact; otherwise it passes through unchanged.

## Golden rule

```bash
# ❌ Wrong
git add . && git commit -m "msg" && git push

# ✅ Correct
rtk git add . && rtk git commit -m "msg" && rtk git push
```

Use `rtk` in every chained command (`&&`, `|`, `;`).

## MeridianERP commands

```bash
# Git / GitHub
rtk git status
rtk git diff
rtk git log --oneline -5
rtk gh pr checks

# Package manager & build
rtk pnpm install
rtk pnpm run build
rtk next build

# Tests (this repo)
rtk jest                    # API unit/e2e via jest
rtk playwright test         # e2e/ Playwright
rtk pnpm --filter @meridian/api test:e2e

# Prisma & Docker
rtk prisma migrate dev
rtk docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml ps

# Debug noisy output
rtk err <cmd>               # errors only
rtk proxy <cmd>             # bypass filter when debugging
```

## When to skip RTK

- Interactive commands that need full TUI (`vim`, `less`, `gh auth login`)
- When the user explicitly asks for raw/unfiltered output
